---
title: "Self-hosted Strava Alternative – Free & Open Source | Dreeve"
description: "Looking for a Strava alternative? Dreeve is a free, open-source, self-hosted dashboard for your rides, runs and workouts. Import your Strava archive, Garmin or FIT files and keep your data on your own server."
canonical: "https://dreeve.app/strava-alternative"
robots: "index, follow, max-image-preview:large"
ogTitle: "Coming from Strava? Take your whole training history with you."
ogDescription: "Dreeve is a free, open-source, self-hosted dashboard for your sports data. Import your Strava archive in minutes. No accounts, no ads, no paywall on your own stats."
twitterTitle: "Coming from Strava? Take your whole training history with you."
twitterDescription: "Free, open-source, self-hosted dashboard for your rides, runs and workouts."
twitterImage: "https://dreeve.app/assets/og-image.png"
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}

  <!-- Structured data: software -->
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
    "name": "Dreeve",
    "alternateName": "Statistics for Strava",
    "applicationCategory": "HealthApplication",
    "applicationSubCategory": "Sports and fitness dashboard",
    "operatingSystem": "Docker, Linux, Kubernetes",
    "description": "A free, open-source, self-hosted dashboard for your sports and fitness data. Import activities from FIT, TCX and GPX files, Garmin, Polar, Wahoo, Hammerhead, Zepp or Strava.",
    "url": "https://dreeve.app/",
    "downloadUrl": "{{ site.githubUrl }}",
    "license": "https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "EUR" },
    "sameAs": ["{{ site.githubUrl }}", "https://docs.dreeve.app/"]
  }
  </script>
{%- endblock %}

{% block content %}

<main>
    <section class="bg-white max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-5 pt-10 pb-14 md:pt-14 md:pb-20">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
            <span class="eyebrow">Coming from Strava?</span>
            <h1 class="mt-4 text-[1.75rem] sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-[1.1] tracking-tight max-w-4xl mx-auto">
                The self-hosted Strava alternative that keeps your data <span class="text-strava-orange">yours</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-4 sm:mt-5 text-base md:text-lg text-gray-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
                Dreeve is a free, open-source dashboard for your rides, runs and workouts.
                Bring your entire Strava history with you, keep it on your own server,
                and get every stat without a subscription.
            </p>
            <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600" aria-label="Highlights">
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="check-badge mt-0">
                      <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                    </span>
                    Free forever
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="check-badge mt-0">
                      <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                    </span>
                    Open source (AGPL-3.0)
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="check-badge mt-0">
                      <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                    </span>
                    Self-hosted
                </li>
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
                    <span class="check-badge mt-0">
                      <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m5 12 5 5L20 7"/></svg>
                    </span>
                    No accounts, ads or tracking
                </li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mt-6 sm:mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
                <a href="#migrate" class="btn btn-primary group">
                    Move your Strava data
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:translate-x-1" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
                </a>
                <a href="https://demo.dreeve.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline">
                    Try the live demo
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-3.5 text-gray-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v10a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14"/></svg>
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="relative z-10 mt-12 md:mt-16">
            <div class="window">
                <div class="window-bar">
                    <div class="window-dots">
                        <span></span>
                        <span></span>
                        <span></span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="window-url">
                        <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 15v2m-6 4h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2Zm10-10V7a4 4 0 0 0-8 0v4h8Z"/></svg>
                        demo.dreeve.app
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-1.5 opacity-0"><span class="size-2.5"></span></div>
                </div>
                <img src="assets/dashboard.webp" alt="Dreeve dashboard showing yearly distance, weekly training load, best efforts and an activity heatmap" width="1541" height="767" fetchpriority="high" class="block w-full h-auto"/>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section id="migrate" class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-5 py-14 md:py-20">
        <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Step by step</span>
            <h2 class="mt-4 section-title">How to move your Strava history to Dreeve</h2>
            <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">
                Strava lets every user download a full archive of their account, including the original
                activity files. Dreeve imports those files directly. You don't need a Strava subscription for this.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ol class="mt-10 space-y-4">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <span class="feature-card__icon shrink-0 mb-0 text-sm font-bold">1</span>
                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Request your Strava archive</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
                        On strava.com, go to <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Settings → My Account → Download or Delete Your Account</span>
                        and choose <span class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Request your archive</span>. Strava emails you a download link,
                        usually within a few hours.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <span class="feature-card__icon shrink-0 mb-0 text-sm font-bold">2</span>
                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Install Dreeve</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">If you can run a Docker container, you can run Dreeve: a home server, a NAS or a small VPS all work.</p>
                    <div class="mt-3 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3.5 py-2.5 bg-[#1a1f27] border-b border-white/5">
                            <div class="window-dots">
                                <span></span>
                                <span></span>
                                <span></span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-gray-500 font-mono">bash</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="font-mono bg-[#212730] text-gray-200 px-4 py-3.5 text-[12px] sm:text-[13px] leading-[1.7] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre">$ <span class="text-orange-400">mkdir</span> dreeve &amp;&amp; <span class="text-orange-400">cd</span> dreeve
<span class="text-gray-500"># add docker-compose.yml and .env from the installation guide</span>
$ <span class="text-orange-400">docker</span> compose up -d
<span class="text-gray-500"># then open http://localhost:8080</span></div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">Full instructions are in the <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/getting-started/installation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">installation guide</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <span class="feature-card__icon shrink-0 mb-0 text-sm font-bold">3</span>
                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Unpack your activity files and drop them into the watch folder</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Dreeve reads plain <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.fit</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.tcx</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.gpx</code> files, not compressed
                        archives. Unzip the Strava archive, then decompress the activity files inside it:
                        Strava stores many of them as <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.fit.gz</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.gpx.gz</code> or <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">.tcx.gz</code>.
                        Finally, copy them into Dreeve's <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">watch/</code> folder.
                    </p>
                    <div class="mt-3 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
                        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3.5 py-2.5 bg-[#1a1f27] border-b border-white/5">
                            <div class="window-dots">
                                <span></span>
                                <span></span>
                                <span></span>
                            </div>
                            <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-gray-500 font-mono">bash</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="font-mono bg-[#212730] text-gray-200 px-4 py-3.5 text-[12px] sm:text-[13px] leading-[1.7] overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre">$ <span class="text-orange-400">unzip</span> export_*.zip -d strava-export
$ <span class="text-orange-400">gunzip</span> strava-export/activities/*.gz
$ <span class="text-orange-400">cp</span> strava-export/activities/*.{fit,tcx,gpx} /path/to/dreeve/watch/</div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
                        On Windows or macOS you can use 7-Zip or The Unarchiver instead. FIT files give you the
                        richest data: power, heart rate, laps and full streams.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <span class="feature-card__icon shrink-0 mb-0 text-sm font-bold">4</span>
                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Let Dreeve import everything</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Dreeve checks the folder every five minutes. Duplicates are skipped
                        automatically, so it's safe to re-run. You can follow progress on the import log at
                        <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">/admin/file-imports</code>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <span class="feature-card__icon shrink-0 mb-0 text-sm font-bold">5</span>
                <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                    <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900">Keep new activities flowing in</h3>
                    <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Connect <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/connectors/garmin-connect/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">Garmin Connect</a>,
                        <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/connectors/polar-flow-connector/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">Polar Flow</a>,
                        <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/connectors/wahoo-connector/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">Wahoo</a> or another
                        <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/importing/overview/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">connector</a> so new workouts arrive
                        straight from your device. No Strava in between.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="bg-gray-50 border-y border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-5 py-14 md:py-20">
            <div>
                <h2 class="section-title">Dreeve vs. Strava at a glance</h2>
                <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600">They do different jobs. Strava is a social network for athletes. Dreeve is your private, long-term training archive.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-10 overflow-x-auto rounded-[14px] border border-gray-200 bg-white">
                <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] text-sm text-left">
                    <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-xxs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500">
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-200"><span class="sr-only">Feature</span></th>
                            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 text-strava-orange">Dreeve</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-200">Strava</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-gray-600 [&_td]:px-4 [&_td]:py-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_tr:not(:last-child)_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-gray-200 [&_td:first-child]:font-semibold [&_td:first-child]:text-gray-900 [&_td:first-child]:w-[30%]">
                        <tr><td>Where your data lives</td><td>Your own server</td><td>Strava's cloud</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Price</td><td>Free, no premium tier</td><td>Free plan plus a paid subscription</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Source code</td><td>Open source (AGPL-3.0)</td><td>Proprietary</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Ads &amp; tracking</td><td>None</td><td>See Strava's privacy policy</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Data sources</td><td>FIT/TCX/GPX files, Garmin, Polar, Wahoo, Hammerhead, Zepp, optional Strava sync</td><td>Most devices and apps</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Social feed &amp; kudos</td><td>No: it's your personal dashboard</td><td>Yes</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Segment leaderboards</td><td>Your own segment history</td><td>Global leaderboards</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>Setup</td><td>Docker, a few minutes</td><td>Sign up in the app</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
                Want both?
                With a Strava subscription, Dreeve can also
                <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/importing/strava-import/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">sync directly from Strava</a>,
                including segments, challenges and trophies.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-5 py-14 md:py-20">
        <h2 class="section-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="mt-10 space-y-3">
            <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden font-bold text-gray-900">
                    Is Dreeve a free Strava alternative?
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-strava-orange transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Yes. Dreeve is free and open source under the AGPL-3.0 licence. There is no premium tier and no paywall on any statistic. You run it yourself with Docker.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden font-bold text-gray-900">
                    Do I need a Strava account to use Dreeve?
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-strava-orange transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">No. Dreeve works with plain FIT, TCX and GPX files and with connectors for Garmin Connect, Polar Flow, Wahoo, Hammerhead and Zepp. Strava sync is optional.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden font-bold text-gray-900">
                    Can I keep using Strava alongside Dreeve?
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-strava-orange transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Yes. Many people keep Strava for its social features and use Dreeve as a private, long-term archive and analysis tool. Dreeve can sync from Strava directly if you have a Strava subscription.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden font-bold text-gray-900">
                    Where is my data stored?
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-strava-orange transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">On your own server, in a local database. Dreeve has no user accounts on our side, no tracking and no ads.</p>
            </details>
            <details class="group bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-[14px] p-[18px]">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden font-bold text-gray-900">
                    What do I need to run Dreeve?
                    <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-4 shrink-0 text-strava-orange transition-transform group-open:rotate-45" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
                </summary>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Anything that can run a Docker container: a home server, a NAS, a Raspberry Pi-class machine or a small VPS. <a href="https://docs.dreeve.app/getting-started/installation-on-k8s/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-link">Kubernetes</a> is supported too.</p>
            </details>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="bg-gray-50 border-y border-gray-200">
        {% set communityHtml %}{% include "partials/community.njk" %}{% endset %}{{ communityHtml | trim | safe }}
        <p class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 pb-6 text-center text-xxs text-gray-400">
            Strava is a trademark of Strava, Inc. Dreeve is an independent open-source project and is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Strava.
        </p>
    </section>
</main>
{% endblock %}
